The app uses these npm packages, which are installed from the registry and keep
their own licences: occt-import-js (LGPL-2.1; its JavaScript and WebAssembly are
served to the browser as they are, from node_modules), three.js (MIT), pdf.js
(Apache-2.0), tesseract.js (Apache-2.0; it downloads its OCR engine and English
language data from a CDN when OCR is first used), React (MIT), and the fonts
Schibsted Grotesk and IBM Plex Mono (SIL Open Font License 1.1, via Fontsource).
The Docker image installs KiCad's libraries from Debian's packages (CC-BY-SA 4.0
with the exception above).

The name Crossprobe and its logo (apps/web/public/favicon.svg,
apps/web/src/ui/Logo.tsx) identify the project. The Apache License does not grant
permission to use them for other products (section 6).

No KiCad source code is included. KiCad (GPL-3.0) is used only as an external
program: the app reads KiCad's installed libraries and demos when they are present,
and tests compare results with KiCad's.
